 impressive speed and efficiency in a casual domestic environment.', 'similarity score': 0.6668059229850769}, {'clip_92_96': 'clip_92_96', 'text': 'In this cooking demonstration sequence from the Korean show **"편스토랑" (Pyeonstaurant)**, a woman in a white polo shirt and mint green apron prepares a marinade in a modern kitchen studio.\n\n**Actions:** The woman carefully pours **맛간장** (tasty soy sauce) from a large bottle with a red cap into a stainless steel mixing bowl containing ground meat topped with minced garlic and ginger. The camera transitions from a medium shot of her concentrating face to close-ups of her hands steadily streaming the dark liquid over the ingredients.\n\n**Setting & Objects:** The scene takes place in a clean, organized kitchen with wooden cabinets, stainless steel appliances, and a colorful fruit poster on the wall. Visible items include a mixing spoon, a knife on the counter, and seasoning containers with yellow and white lids beside the bowl. The woman wears a smartwatch on her left wrist.\n\n**Text:** On-screen graphics display the show title "편스토랑," menu text referencing "1인용 된장 보쌈과" (single serving soybean paste bossam), and the prominent yellow text "맛간장" identifying the ingredient being added.\n\n**Mood:** The atmosphere is calm, methodical, and professional—typical of an instructional cooking segment—with the woman\'s focused expression emphasizing careful seasoning and preparation technique.', 'similarity score': 0.660186767578125}, {'clip_91_92': 'clip_91_92', 'text': 'In this brief sequence from a cooking show, a woman in a white shirt and light green apron stands at a modern kitchen counter with dark wood cabinetry and stainless steel appliances. At 91s, she holds a bottle with a red cap (soy sauce) over a large metal mixing bowl, appearing to prepare ingredients for a recipe. The camera then zooms in at 92s as she looks down to pour or measure the liquid. Large yellow Korean text appears on screen reading **"맛간장"** (seasoned/flavored soy sauce), identifying the ingredient being used. The setting includes various kitchen appliances visible in the background, including a refrigerator with a colorful poster and a coffee machine. The mood is instructional and focused, typical of a cooking demonstration segment.', 'similarity score': 0.6591065526008606}, {'clip_4_9': 'clip_4_9', 'text': 'In a modern kitchen with white cabinets and wood flooring, a woman in a cream blouse and jeans carries a heavy black reusable shopping bag to a white dining table, visibly straining as on-screen text reads **"아휴 무거워"** (Ah, heavy). The camera shifts to an overhead view showing her unpacking the bag, which features yellow text reading **"AND THINK SAVE A LIFE!"** She pulls out multiple packages of tofu (두부), with the text updating to **"두부 4모"** (4 blocks of tofu) as she lines them up on the table. The sequence includes picture-in-picture commentary from a male speaker (frame 6) and a female speaker (frame 9) in the bottom left corner. The show title **"편스토랑"** appears in the top left throughout. The mood is light and domestic, emphasizing the considerable weight and quantity of groceries.', 'similarity score': 0.6589370369911194}, {'clip_229_232': 'clip_229_232', 'text': 'In this cooking demonstration sequence, a woman in a mint green apron demonstrates how to dehydrate salted vegetables. \n\n**Frame 1 (229s):** A split-screen shows a close-up of a metal bowl filled with sliced white radish on the left, and the instructor on the right adding salt to a bowl. On-screen text reads "소금 살짝" (a little salt). The show title "편스토랑" and programme information appear at the top.\n\n**Frame 2 (230s):** A close-up shows the instructor lifting a white cloth or cheesecloth over a metal bowl, preparing to wrap the contents.\n\n**Frames 3-4 (231-232s):** The instructor wraps the bowl tightly with the white cloth to squeeze out excess moisture. The text "무를 짜봅시다" (Let\'s squeeze the radish) appears on screen. In the final frame, a small inset shows a male commentator reacting to the demonstration. The instructor wears a smartwatch on her left wrist throughout the process.\n\nThe setting is a modern kitchen studio, and the mood is practical and instructional, typical of a cooking competition or tutorial show.', 'similarity score': 0.6552461981773376}, {'clip_133_137': 'clip_133_137', 'text': 'In this kitchen cooking segment, a woman demonstrates how to remove excess moisture from tofu. \n\n**Actions:** The sequence begins with a close-up of hands holding tofu wrapped in a white cloth (133s). The woman then stands at a kitchen sink, vigorously squeezing and twisting the cloth bundle with both hands to extract liquid (134s-136s). By 137s, she continues squeezing with focused effort while a small inset shows a male commentator laughing heartily at the scene.\n\n**People/Objects:** The main subject is a woman with dark hair tied back, wearing a white short-sleeved shirt and a sage green apron, plus a smartwatch. She handles a white cloth pouch containing tofu over a stainless steel sink. A large metal bowl filled with chopped green vegetables sits on the counter beside her.\n\n**Setting:** A modern domestic kitchen featuring white countertops, dark cabinetry, a stainless steel refrigerator, and various cooking ingredients and tools arranged on the counter.\n\n**Visible Text:** Korean text appears throughout: in the top-left corner reads "편스토랑" (show title), while the top banner displays "13번째 참가자" (13th participant) and "황금 레시피 만능 100배." The first frame includes instructional text: "수분이 많은 두부는 면포에 싸서 물기를 제거" (Tofu with lots of moisture—wrap in cloth to remove water).\n\n**Mood:** Practical and instructional, shifting to lighthearted in the final frame due to the laughing reaction shot.', 'similarity score': 0.6520665884017944}, {'clip_220_226': 'clip_220_226', 'text': 'In this sequence from a Korean cooking show, a woman with her hair tied back in a ponytail, wearing a light-colored polo shirt, is preparing food in a modern kitchen equipped with a washing machine and various appliances.\n\nThe segment begins with a medium shot of her standing at the kitchen counter, then transitions to close-up shots of her hands working with ingredients in a large stainless steel bowl. She is mixing a generous amount of finely shredded white vegetables (appearing to be Korean radish/mu) with her bare hands, fluffing and tossing the strands to ensure even distribution.\n\nOn-screen Korean text appears throughout: the first caption mentions "천연 소화제 무가 들어가 깔끔하고 속도 편한 무만두" (moo/dumplings with natural digestive enzymes that are clean and comfortable for digestion). Later text on frames 223-226 reads "두 번째 채쓸기까지 완료" indicating the completion of the second round of cutting/shredding the vegetables.\n\nThe mood is practical and instructional, typical of a cooking demonstration, with the focus on the tactile preparation of ingredients.', 'similarity score': 0.6520429253578186}, {'clip_115_118': 'clip_115_118', 'text': 'In this cooking demonstration sequence, a person prepares a dish by mixing chopped green vegetables with a ground meat filling in a stainless steel bowl set on a white kitchen counter near a sink. \n\n**Frame 115s:** The metal bowl sits on the counter, containing a mixture of what appears to be ground meat on the left and a pile of freshly chopped green herbs (likely garlic chives or scallions) on the right. Korean show graphics appear in the top-left corner, including the title "편스토랑" (Pyeon\'s Restaurant).\n\n**Frame 116s:** A person\'s hands—wearing a smartwatch with a brown leather band on the left wrist—add another portion of chopped greens into the bowl. On-screen text reads "두 움큼" (meaning "two handfuls").\n\n**Frame 117s:** The shot shifts to a wooden cutting board where the person gathers a generous double handful of the finely chopped green vegetables, with a knife resting beside remaining chopped piles.\n\n**Frame 118s:** The hands transfer the gathered