, 'similarity score': 0.5644699335098267}, {'clip_460_462': 'clip_460_462', 'text': 'In this cooking sequence from a Korean culinary show (*Pyeonstaurant*), the focus is on **mandu** (dumpling) preparation. \n\n**Frames at 460-461s:** Close-up shots show a workstation with a metal mixing bowl containing savory filling (chopped vegetables and protein) on the left, and a clear plastic container holding water—used for sealing mandu wrappers—at center. Korean text reads *"빠르게 사라지는 만두피"* ("Mandu wrappers disappearing quickly"), suggesting rapid consumption or usage of the dough sheets.\n\n**Frame at 462s:** The camera shifts to an overhead view revealing the full workspace: a white cutting board with filling, arranged wrappers, and a person\'s hands actively folding dumplings. Bold red text announces *"세 번째 판 완성"* ("Third tray/batch complete"). A picture-in-picture insert at bottom left shows commentator **Choi Ye-seul** reacting to the progress.\n\n**Setting:** A clean, organized kitchen with wooden flooring and minimalist white furniture. **Mood:** Productive and satisfying, emphasizing the steady, rhythmic progress of handmade dumpling preparation.', 'similarity score': 0.5641084909439087}, {'clip_238_243': 'clip_238_243', 'text': 'In this sequence from the Korean cooking show **"Pyeonstorang"** (편스토랑), a woman in a white collared shirt and light sage apron demonstrates how to squeeze moisture from dumpling filling.\n\n**The Action:** The sequence begins with a close-up (238s) showing hands gathering white filling (likely tofu or vegetables) into a large white cheesecloth over a metal bowl. The camera then cuts to medium shots (239s-243s) of the woman vigorously twisting the cloth bundle with both hands, wringing out excess liquid. Her expressions shift from focused concentration to cheerful determination, smiling and slightly grimacing (240s-242s) as she applies significant physical force, before looking down with a satisfied smile (243s).\n\n**Setting & Objects:** T