Caption search results: [{'clip_163_167': 'clip_163_167', 'text': 'In this kitchen scene, a woman wearing a light green apron and a smartwatch prepares ingredients by dehydrating them using a manual method. \n\n**163s–164s:** Close-up shots show her hands wrapping ingredients (likely bean sprouts, per the on-screen Korean text *"대체 숙주도 면포에 올려주고"*) in a white cotton cloth over a glass bowl. A large metal bowl filled with chopped green vegetables sits nearby on the counter.\n\n**165s–167s:** The camera pulls back to reveal the woman twisting and squeezing the cloth bundle with both hands to extract liquid, acting as a manual press. She wrings it tightly over the bowl, demonstrating significant effort. \n\n**Setting & Text:** The modern kitchen features a washing machine, gas stove, and wooden cutting board. Korean text overlays include *"인간 탈수기"* (Human dehydrator) humorously describing her action, and *"타지 등장"* (Dashi appears/enters), suggesting she\'s preparing stock. The mood is focused and domestic, typical of a cooking demonstration.', 'similarity score': 0.7500925064086914}, {'clip_243_248': 'clip_243_248', 'text': 'In this cooking demonstration sequence from the Korean show *Pyeonstaurant* (편스토랑), a woman in a white shirt and light green apron strains liquid from a white cloth bag (likely containing a blended or soaked ingredient) into a clear glass bowl. \n\n**Actions:** The woman firmly twists and squeezes the cloth bag with both hands, extracting a thick white liquid that streams into the bowl below. The on-screen text "콸콸" (an onomatopoeia for pouring liquid) appears during the squeezing action.\n\n**Visual Details:** The close-up shots focus on her hands—one wearing a smartwatch with a black band—working the bag over a kitchen counter with metal bowls visible in the background. \n\n**Setting:** The scene takes place in a bright kitchen studio environment.\n\n**Additional Elements:** Small picture-in-picture boxes in the bottom right corner show commentators reacting: first a man in a dark blue outfit, then switching to a man in a red outfit who gestures as he speaks.\n\n**Mood:** The atmosphere is calm and instructional, with the woman smiling gently at the beginning, suggesting a lighthearted cooking competition atmosphere.', 'similarity score': 0.7388992309570312}, {'clip_217_220': 'clip_217_220', 'text': 'In this cooking demonstration sequence from the Korean show *Pyeon Restaurant* (편스토랑), a woman in a light green apron and white shirt prepares ingredients for radish dumplings (무만두).\n\n**Actions & Objects:** The sequence begins with close-ups of her hands rapidly slicing white radish (무) using a pink mandoline slicer over a large stainless steel mixing bowl (217s-218s). The slicing is quick and efficient. The scene then cuts to wider shots (219s-220s) showing her standing at a kitchen counter, pausing briefly with the tool in hand before turning slightly to reach for another item.\n\n**Setting:** The kitchen is modern and compact, featuring a sink, cutting board, range hood, and a washing machine visible in the background. Various cooking utensils and bottles are arranged on the counter.\n\n**Text:** On-screen Korean text reads: *"천연 소화제 무가 들어가 깔끔하고 속도 편한 무만두"* ("Radish, a natural digestive aid, goes in—clean and conveniently speedy radish dumplings"). The show\'s logo (*편스토랑*) appears in the top-left corner with the episode theme mentioning a dumpling competition. A small inset image of the woman is visible in the bottom-left corner.\n\n**Mood:** The atmosphere is focused and efficient, emphasizing the convenience and speed of the preparation method for making healthy homemade dumplings.', 'similarity score': 0.7260446548461914}, {'clip_271_283': 'clip_271_283', 'text': 'In this cooking show segment (from the Korean program "편스토랑"), a woman in a white shirt and light green apron prepares dumpling filling in a modern kitchen setting.\n\n**Frames 271–272**: A triptych shows her adding ingredients to a large metal