-screen graphics read **"1인자를 위한 비상금 / 망년회 코스지! ●만두"** (Emergency fund for the #1 / Year-end party course! ● Dumplings).\n\n**Mood:** The atmosphere is lighthearted and industrious, emphasizing the physical effort required in traditional cooking preparation while maintaining a pleasant, engaging tone.', 'similarity score': 0.7094330191612244}, {'clip_115_118': 'clip_115_118', 'text': 'In this cooking demonstration sequence, a person prepares a dish by mixing chopped green vegetables with a ground meat filling in a stainless steel bowl set on a white kitchen counter near a sink. \n\n**Frame 115s:** The metal bowl sits on the counter, containing a mixture of what appears to be ground meat on the left and a pile of freshly chopped green herbs (likely garlic chives or scallions) on the right. Korean show graphics appear in the top-left corner, including the title "편스토랑" (Pyeon\'s Restaurant).\n\n**Frame 116s:** A person\'s hands—wearing a smartwatch with a brown leather band on the left wrist—add another portion of chopped greens into the bowl. On-screen text reads "두 움큼" (meaning "two handfuls").\n\n**Frame 117s:** The shot shifts to a wooden cutting board where the person gathers a generous double handful of the finely chopped green vegetables, with a knife resting beside remaining chopped piles.\n\n**Frame 118s:** The hands transfer the gathered greens into the bowl, beginning to combine them with the meat mixture.\n\nThe setting is a bright, clean kitchen environment typical of a cooking show, with a calm, instructional mood focused on the food preparation process.', 'similarity score': 0.7064817547798157}, {'clip_133_137': 'clip_133_137', 'text': 'In this kitchen cooking segment, a woman demonstrates how to remove excess moisture from tofu. \n\n**Actions:** The sequence begins with a close-up of hands holding tofu wrapped in a white cloth (133s). The woman then stands at a kitchen sink, vigorously squeezing and twisting the cloth bundle with both hands to extract liquid (134s-136s). By 137s, she continues squeezing with focused effort while a small inset shows a male commentator laughing heartily at the scene.\n\n**People/Objects:** The main subject is a woman with dark hair tied back, wearing a white short-sleeved shirt and a sage green apron, plus a smartwatch. She handles a white cloth pouch containing tofu over a stainless steel sink. A large metal bowl filled with chopped green vegetables sits on the counter beside her.\n\n**Setting:** A modern domestic kitchen featuring white countertops, dark cabinetry, a stainless steel refrigerator, and various cooking ingredients and tools arranged on the counter.\n\n**Visible Text:** Korean text appears throughout: in the top-left corner reads "편스토랑" (show title), while the top banner displays "13번째 참가자" (13th participant) and "황금 레시피 만능 100배." The first frame includes instructional text: "수분이 많은 두부는 면포에 싸서 물기를 제거" (Tofu with lots of moisture—wrap in cloth to remove water).\n\n**Mood:** Practical and instructional, shifting to lighthearted in the final frame due to the laughing reaction shot.', 'similarity score': 0.703357458114624}, {'clip_110_115': 'clip_110_115', 'text': '**Setting & Context:** A split-screen cooking demonstration (likely from a Korean TV show called "편스토랑" / "Pyeonstorang") in a modern kitchen studio, focusing on dumpling preparation ("13년째 만두쇼" - 13th Year Dumpling Show).\n\n**Sequence of Actions:**\n- **110s-111s:** A woman in a white shirt and sage green apron finely chops garlic chives (부추) on a wooden cutting board. The right panel shows a close-up of the knife technique labeled "부추 2단 썰기" (cutting chives in two stages/sections). She wears a smartwatch on her left wrist.\n- **112s-113s:** Using both hands ("두손"), she scoops up the chopped chives ("가득" - full handful) from the board.\n- **114s-115s:** She transfers the chopped chives into a large stainless steel mixing bowl containing ground meat, placing the greens beside the meat mixture near a kitchen si